# Paste your ADMIN PUBLIC keys here (one per line), then save this file as
#   authorized_keys   (drop the .example).
#
# These are PUBLIC keys — safe to carry on the USB.  They let your admin
# machines SSH INTO any box you onboard.  Do NOT put private keys here.
#
# Get a machine's public key with:   cat ~/.ssh/id_ed25519.pub
# (or the .pub that matches whatever key your admins use to connect).
#
# Example line (replace with your real key):
# ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAA...replace-me... ct-admin@cthome
